{"qid":"Q487829","names":["Chagatai Khanate"],"title":"Chagatai Khanate","endonym":{"native":"Цагаадайн Улс","lang":"mn"},"capsule":"The Chagatai Khanate was the Mongol successor state assigned to Chagatai Khan, second son of Genghis Khan, encompassing the former Qara Khitai and Karluk territories from the Amu Darya to the Altai Mountains; it is attested in the dataset from 1294, after the fragmentation of the unified Mongol Empire. The khanate developed a persistent tension between its sedentary western half (Transoxiana, centred on Samarkand and Bukhara) and its nomadic eastern half (Moghulistan), which effectively split into two polities by the mid-fourteenth century. The western Chagataid lands were conquered by Timur (Tamerlane) between 1370 and 1390, who extinguished Chagataid rule west of the Tian Shan; the eastern remnant, Moghulistan, survived as a diminished khanate, with the last Chagataid ruler of the unified polity recognized by the dataset to 1462.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The khanate's general territory in Central Asia is established by Persian chronicles and Mongol administrative records; precise boundaries fluctuated substantially with seasonal pasturage and competing khanate claims, and frontier zones with the Ilkhanate, Yuan, and Golden Horde are approximate in all reconstructions.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Chagatai Khanate","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Chagatai-khanate"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Chagatai Khanate","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chagatai_Khanate"}],"britannica":"place/Chagatai-Khanate","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Chagatai Khanate","rulers":[{"qid":"Q1341135","name":"Duwa","nativeName":"Дува хаан","roman":"Duwa","start":1282,"end":1307,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Könchek","nativeName":"Хөнчег","roman":"Könchek","start":1307,"end":1308,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Taliqu","nativeName":"Талигу","roman":"Taliqu","start":1308,"end":1309,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Kebek","nativeName":"Хэбэг хаан","roman":"Kebek","start":1309,"end":1309,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Esen Buqa I","nativeName":"Эсэн Бух","roman":"Esen Buqa I","start":1309,"end":1318,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Kebek (restored)","nativeName":"Хэбэг хаан","roman":"Kebek","start":1318,"end":1325,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Eljigidey","nativeName":"Элжигидэй","roman":"Eljigidey","start":1325,"end":1329,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Duwa Temür","nativeName":"Дува Төмөр","roman":"Duwa Temür","start":1329,"end":1330,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Tarmashirin","nativeName":"Тармаширин хаан","roman":"Tarmashirin","start":1331,"end":1334,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Buzan","nativeName":"Бузан","roman":"Buzan","start":1334,"end":1335,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Changshi","nativeName":"Чанши","roman":"Changshi","start":1335,"end":1338,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Yesün Temür","nativeName":"Есөн Төмөр","roman":"Yesün Temür","start":1338,"end":1342,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Muhammad I","nativeName":"Мухаммед","roman":"Muhammad","start":1342,"end":1343,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Qazan","nativeName":"Хазан хаан","ro